  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Cut the Padron peppers in half and remove the seeds and membranes.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the onion and garlic to the pot and cook for 5 minutes, until softened.",
    "Add the tomato paste to the pot and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the German beer to the pot and cook for 2 minutes, until slightly reduced.",
    "Add the chicken broth, thyme, salt, and black pepper to the pot.",
    "Stir to combine, then add the Padron peppers to the pot.",
    "Cover the pot with a lid and transfer it to the preheated oven.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, until the peppers are tender and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Serve the peppers hot, garnished with chopped fresh parsley if desired."
  ],
